PASSWD(1)

NAME
    passwd - set or clear a SmallOS shadow password

SYNOPSIS
    passwd [user]
    passwd -d user

DESCRIPTION
    passwd is the native SmallOS password utility. With no user argument it
    updates the current user's /etc/shadow entry. Root may name another user.

    Password entry disables terminal echo. Empty new passwords and mismatched
    confirmation entries are rejected.

    Passwords are stored in /etc/shadow with the SmallOS-only hash format:

        $smallos-sha256$<salt>$<hex-digest>

    Salt generation uses available time, pid, uid, and rand() state. This is
    sufficient for the current SmallOS milestone, but it is not production-grade
    entropy and is not compatible with Linux crypt hash formats.

    Root can clear a password for development recovery:

        passwd -d root

FILES
    /bin/passwd
    /etc/passwd
    /etc/shadow

SEE ALSO
    login(1), shell(1), smallos(7)
